course: dictionary
lesson: 12500
title: Dependent: needing or changing with something else
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dependent comes from the verb depend. When something is dependent on something else, it needs that thing or changes because of it. «Babies are dependent on their parents for food and warmth.» A baby cannot survive alone, so it needs its parents for help.
explain: «Our picnic is dependent on the weather.» The picnic might change if the weather changes. Check it by swapping in the words depends on: «Our picnic depends on the weather» still makes sense, so dependent is the right meaning.
explain: In science, a dependent variable is what you measure. In a plant test, you change the amount of water and measure how tall the plant grows. The height depends on the water, so height is the dependent variable.
explain: A dependent can also be a noun. It means a person, usually a child, who relies on someone else for money and care. «He has three dependants.» Americans spell it dependent; British English usually spells it dependant.
fact: Dependent means needing someone or something else for help, money or care.
fact: Dependent can also mean changing because of something else: «Our trip is dependent on the weather.»
fact: In science, the dependent variable is what you measure, and it changes when you change something else.
fact: A dependent (noun) is usually a child who relies on someone for money and care.
fact: Common phrases include «dependent on», «dependent upon» and «heavily dependent».
exercise: «Babies are dependent on their parents.» What does dependent mean here? | Able to look after themselves | *Needing someone for help and care | Very tall for their age | Happy to be alone
exercise: «Our picnic is dependent on the weather.» What does this mean? | Nobody cares about the picnic | The weather is always the same | *The picnic will change depending on the weather | The picnic is in the weather
exercise: In a plant test, Priya changes the water and measures how tall the plant grows. Which is the dependent variable? | The day of the week | The amount of water | *How tall the plant grows | The type of pot
test: «Ravi is dependent on his parents for money.» What does this mean? | He lends money to his parents | He works at the bank | He has lots of money of his own | *He relies on his parents for money
test: Which word names a person, usually a child, who relies on someone for money and care? | a departure | a dependable friend | a deposit | *a dependent
exam: «The price of the ticket is dependent on how many you buy.» What does dependent mean here? | It is paid by someone else | It is free for everyone | *It changes with how many you buy | It is always the same price
